From 302f1d9c3d97890d028b5c98ecf1e4eb1749ba57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:16:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] GUIFadeLabelControl: draw scrolling text with the depth of
 the pass it is drawn in

Kodi processes every control, then assigns the depths of the pass (CGUIWindowManager:
AssignDepth() after Process()), then renders. The fade label makes the matrix it renders its
scrolling text with in Process(), and gives it the depth that AssignDepth() kept in the pass
before: AssignDepth() updated m_fadeDepth and not the matrix. Render() then drew with the depth
of the previous pass. The depth is normalised with the layers of the current pass
(CGraphicContext::GetNormalizedDepth()) and the vertex shaders write it to z: where the layers
went down from one pass to the next, the text could end beyond the far plane and be clipped,
even with the depth test off (Kodi's default). Also found by the fork of CroqueMr (PR #48).

AssignDepth() now sets the depth of the matrix too. Host test (the real
GUIFadeLabelControl.cpp against stand-ins of what it uses, six passes whose depth goes up and
down): before, five of six passes drawn with another pass's depth; after, none.
---
 xbmc/guilib/GUIFadeLabelControl.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/guilib/GUIFadeLabelControl.cpp b/xbmc/guilib/GUIFadeLabelControl.cpp
index 8866ef6..aa53e56 100644
--- a/xbmc/guilib/GUIFadeLabelControl.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/guilib/GUIFadeLabelControl.cpp
@@ -258,6 +258,8 @@ void CGUIFadeLabelControl::AssignDepth()
 {
   CGUIControl::AssignDepth();
   m_fadeDepth = m_cachedTransform.depth;
+  // the matrix that Render() draws with was made in Process(), before the depths of this pass
+  m_fadeMatrix.depth = m_fadeDepth;
 }
 
 std::string CGUIFadeLabelControl::GetDescription() const
